identifier: cas:5743-04-4
preferred_term: Cadmium acetate dihydrate
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:232796
  ontology_label: cadmium acetate
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CultureBotHT
    notes: 'Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 5743-04-4 present, but no CHEBI entry
      exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Used in 1 CultureBot
      media; samples: FW104 COMM. Curator can promote to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI
      adds the term.'
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CHEBI via PubChem (pubchem-xref)
    notes: Parent class identified via pubchem-xref; matched_via='pubchem CID 10986'
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:232796 (''cadmium acetate'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:
      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#321)
    notes: molecular_formula 'C4H6CdO4' -> 'C4H6CdO4.2H2O'. The recorded value described
      the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by
      18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 2 water(s) of hydration,
      and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:232796's
      ChEBI formula ('2C2H3O2.Cd') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent
      rather than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated
      notation.
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'Source CAS5743-04-4 plus supplier/PubChem confirms cadmium acetate dihydrate;
      keep own CAS distinct from CHEBI232796 dry parent. Change quality to NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch
      to232796; no exact dry-parent identity. Retain C4H6CdO4.2H2O and CAS. Withdraw
      dry SMILES, dry InChI and CID10986; fresh dihydrate CID6537495 demonstrates
      the mismatch but is not automatically imported as replacement. Primary source
      references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/mm/102003; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/5743-04-4/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON;
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/232796/. Captures, exact
      input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      Independent review identifies the existing exact synonym ''cadmium(2+);diacetate''
      as the water-free parent, not this hydrate; preserve it as REJECTED_LABEL. This
      curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed owner
      bytes withdraw inherited support.'
synonyms:
